<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 145 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 145 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 145 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>All 145 million stg was in outright bills maturing on or before May 13.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided total liquidity of 865 million stg to the money market to tackle a forecast shortage of 850 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
